#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) ion acoustic wave (IAW) test.
A single-wavelength ion density perturbation is seeded along x in a uniform,
Maxwellian, zero-bulk-velocity proton plasma that is UNMAGNETIZED (B = 0
everywhere).  The electric field is initially zero; the restoring force is the
electron pressure gradient in the generalized Ohm's law (electronTemperature > 0),
which gives the acoustic speed c_s = sqrt(gamma*Te/mi).

  n(x) = n0 * (1 + pert * sin(kx * x)),   kx = 2*pi*waveMode / Lx

The seed is implemented by the C++ TESTCASE IonAcousticWave, which scales each
particle's weight so the deposited ion density carries the sinusoidal profile
while keeping the bulk velocity uniform.

Parameters:
  * gamma = 5/3 (adiabatic electrons);  electronTemperature = 62.8 eV gives
    c_s ~ 1 in code units (Te/mi = 0.6) at uNormSI = 1.0e5.
  * T = 4e5 K gives v_thi ~ 0.58, so c_s / v_thi ~ 1.73.
  * Lx = 16 d_i, nx = 48 -> k d_i = 2*pi/16 = 0.393.
  * pert = 0.02.
  * dt = 0.02.
  * eta = 0, no hyper-resistivity -> the only damping is collisionless ion
    Landau damping. With B = 0 the Hall and convection terms vanish, so the
    Ohm's law reduces to E = -grad(p_e)/rho (the ambipolar field).

FAST regression: TimeMax = 5 s (tNorm = 1 s -> 5 code units ~ 0.3 of the n=1
ion-acoustic period ~ 16 s), nParticle = 2000/cell -> ~1 minute serial run.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-8.0                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 16 d_i]
 8.0                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
48                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
48                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Electron pressure gradient (ambipolar restoring force for the IAW).
electronDensity0 is in amu/cc, the SAME unit as the UNIFORMSTATE rho input, so
set it equal to rho here (both 1.0 amu/cc); the code auto-normalizes both to
code units so the adiabatic closure
p_e = electronDensity0*Te*(rho/electronDensity0)^gamma stays consistent.
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
62.8                    electronTemperature  [eV]
1.6666666666666667      electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0  [amu/cc, same as UNIFORMSTATE rho]

B = 0 so the Hall term (J x B)/rho and the convection term -u_i x B both vanish;
The only remaining E source is the electron pressure gradient -grad(p_e)/rho.
#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm
#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Smoothing of the ion fluid moments (density and momentum) before the Ohm's law
(nSmoothMoments = 2 binomial passes).
#SMOOTHMOMENTS
T                       doSmoothMoments
2                       nSmoothMoments
0.5                     coefSmoothMoments

Smoothing of the cell-centred electric field after each hybrid field advance.
The ambipolar term E = -grad(p_e)/rho uses a central difference that does not
couple odd/even cells, so without this a grid-scale (Nyquist) checkerboard can
grow in E and feed back into the ion push.
#SMOOTHE
T                       doSmoothE
2                       nSmoothE

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
1.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
400000.0                T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]         UNMAGNETIZED Bx0 = 0
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
IonAcousticWave
0.02                    pert       relative density-perturbation amplitude (< 1)
1                       waveMode   number of wavelengths across the x-domain

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
50                      dn
0.0                     dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
5.0                     TimeMax   ~0.3 of the n=1 ion-acoustic period

#RUN

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB
